Fabric Connection persistence outcomes
======================================

A chain's final database commit is part of its reported outcome. An exception
or lost acknowledgement now returns success=false, error_code=COMMIT_FAILED and
commit_status=unconfirmed. The response and Connection-run recorder retain the
individual step results, and diagnostics omit database exception details.

The session attempts rollback and closes. Rollback is best effort, and a failed
commit reply does not establish whether the database committed. This change
cannot undo an external webhook, notification, camera action or a staged change
that another service already committed. It does not add automatic retries;
shared event claims remain intact to avoid blindly repeating uncertain effects.
Operators must reconcile the affected records/effects before deliberately retrying.

This fixes false successful run outcomes. It does not provide a transactional
outbox, exactly-once effects, durable event delivery, atomic multi-step changes
or durable run auditing while the database itself is unavailable. Cancellation
still propagates rather than being converted into a successful result.
